---
import artistPortrait from '../assets/artist-portrait.jpg';
import ArtworkImage from '../components/ArtworkImage.astro';
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { getSortedArtworks } from '../lib/artworks';

const artworks = await getSortedArtworks();
const processArtwork = artworks.find((artwork) => artwork.data.images.some((image) => image.type === 'process'));
const processImage = processArtwork?.data.images.find((image) => image.type === 'process');
---

<BaseLayout title="About the Artist" description="How a midnight experiment became Endeavor Art Studio.">
  <header class="page-header page-shell">
    <p class="eyebrow">About / Artist and practice</p>
    <h1>About the Artist</h1>
  </header>

  <p class="lede large-copy page-shell">Creativity has a way of revealing itself when you least expect it.</p>

  <section class="bio page-shell">
    <figure>
      <ArtworkImage
        src={artistPortrait}
        alt="Illustrated portrait of Chelsea in a pink beret riding an electric scooter past flames"
        sizes="(min-width: 768px) 42vw, 100vw"
        loading="eager"
      />
      <figcaption>Chelsea, artist</figcaption>
    </figure>
    <div>
      <p>Growing up surrounded by artistic talent, I never considered myself an artist. While creativity came naturally to those around me, I had yet to discover a medium that felt like my own.</p>
      <p>During a difficult time in my life, I found myself searching for a creative outlet. Inspired by the work of other artists and driven by little more than curiosity, I began wondering what I might be capable of creating.</p>
      <p>One night, just after midnight, I picked up a blank canvas and decided to find out.</p>
      <p>What began as a spontaneous experiment evolved into a three-month creative process and ultimately became my first original piece, <a href="/artwork/endeavor/">Endeavor</a>. Imperfect, unconventional, and entirely unplanned, it represented the discovery of something I never knew I was capable of.</p>
      <p>That single experience opened the door to an entirely new creative world.</p>
      <p>As my curiosity expanded, so did my work. I began exploring different materials, techniques, and forms, eventually creating distinctive mixed-media pieces and transforming unexpected objects into original works of art. What started as a personal creative outlet gradually developed into a business as others began connecting with and purchasing my work.</p>
      <p>Today, Endeavor represents the same spirit of exploration that inspired its beginning. Each piece is individually conceived and created, combining texture, dimension, and unconventional materials to produce artwork that is as unique as the space it inhabits.</p>
      <p class="bio-close">What began as an experiment became an identity. And the endeavor continues.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="statement section page-shell" aria-labelledby="statement-title">
    <div>
      <h2 id="statement-title" class="section-label">Artist statement</h2>
      <span class="draft-note">Draft for artist review</span>
    </div>
    <div>
      <p class="large-copy">I am drawn to materials that already carry evidence of use, breakage, pressure, and change.</p>
      <div class="statement-columns">
        <p>Temporary first-person copy: The work develops through handling. Glass, ceramic, resin, found objects, and built-up surfaces are tested against one another until their familiar purpose gives way to a new relationship.</p>
        <p>Temporary first-person copy: Fragments are not treated as damage to hide. Their edges, gaps, and points of contact become part of the composition. Experimentation remains visible in the finished piece.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="process" aria-labelledby="process-title">
    {processImage && (
      <div class="process-image">
        <ArtworkImage
          src={processImage.src}
          alt={processImage.alt}
          caption="Process photograph"
          sizes="(min-width: 768px) 62vw, 100vw"
          lightbox
          gallery="artist-process"
        />
      </div>
    )}
    <div class="process-copy">
      <h2 id="process-title" class="section-label">Artistic process</h2>
      <span class="draft-note">Draft for artist review</span>
      <h3>Collect. Test. Break. Reassemble.</h3>
      <p>Materials may suggest the initial direction, but the outcome is not fixed in advance. Construction, removal, and revision continue until the surface and structure feel resolved.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .lede {
    margin-block: 0;
    padding-block: clamp(3rem, 6vw, 6rem);
    text-align: center;
    text-wrap: balance;
  }

  .bio {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 0.85fr) minmax(20rem, 1.15fr);
    gap: clamp(3rem, 8vw, 10rem);
    align-items: start;
    padding-bottom: var(--section-space);
  }

  /* The story runs much taller than the portrait, so the portrait stays in view beside it. */
  .bio figure {
    position: sticky;
    top: 2rem;
    margin: 0;
  }

  .bio figcaption {
    padding-top: 0.5rem;
    color: var(--paper-muted);
    font-size: 0.68rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.12em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  .bio > div > p {
    max-width: 38rem;
    color: var(--paper-muted);
  }

  .bio > div > p.bio-close {
    margin-top: 2.5rem;
    color: var(--paper);
    font-family: var(--serif);
    font-size: 1.5em;
    line-height: 1.3;
  }

  .statement {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 2fr;
    gap: 3rem;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
  }

  .statement-columns {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
    gap: clamp(2rem, 5vw, 6rem);
    margin-top: 4rem;
    color: var(--paper-muted);
  }

  .process {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1.5fr) minmax(20rem, 0.8fr);
    align-items: center;
    background: var(--charcoal);
  }

  .process-image :global(img) {
    width: 100%;
    max-height: 90svh;
    object-fit: cover;
  }

  .process-copy {
    padding: clamp(3rem, 7vw, 8rem) var(--page-pad);
  }

  .process-copy h3 {
    margin-bottom: 2rem;
  }

  @media (max-width: 47.99rem) {
    .bio,
    .statement,
    .process {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }

    .bio figure {
      position: static;
      width: calc(100% + var(--page-pad) * 2);
      margin-left: calc(var(--page-pad) * -1);
    }

    .bio figcaption {
      padding-left: var(--page-pad);
    }

    .statement-columns {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      margin-top: 2rem;
    }

    .process-copy {
      padding-block: 5rem;
    }
  }
</style>
